mido: also pull the shared cache back to its nominal addresses

0125 dropped the slide and VM_PROT_SLIDE from every mapping, and the cache was
then mapped with no pager and no rebase chain -- but launchd died on the very
next syscall:

  MIDO SR 0125: noslide, dyld slide 0x0 dropped for 0 file(s), 0 slid mappings
  MIDO SR: launchd check_np -> 0x183514000
  pid 1 exited -- exit reason namespace 2 subcode 0x0, description none
  panic: initproc failed to start -- exit reason namespace 2 ...

(namespace 2 is OS_REASON_SIGNAL, i.e. launchd took a fault.)

The mistake is that dyld does not hand the kernel an unslid address and let it
add the slide.  It folds the slide into sms_address itself, and passes the slide
separately only so the kernel knows how far to relocate the *contents*:

  nominal base                      0x180000000   (SHARED_REGION_BASE_ARM64)
  dyld's requested slide            0x03514000
  address dyld asks for             0x183514000
  check_np() after 0125             0x183514000   (= base + sr_first_mapping)

So clearing the slide left the cache moved by 0x3514000 but not relocated: the
mapping sits at nominal+slide, dyld reads that base back, still computes a slide
of 0x3514000, and the first shared-cache pointer it dereferences is 0x3514000
off.  Zeroing the slide without moving the mapping is worse than doing nothing.

Fix: derive the slide from the addresses (lowest mapping minus the region base,
which is what sr_first_mapping ends up being) and subtract it from every
sms_address.  sf_slide cannot be used for this: 0123 already zeroes it in the BSD
layer before this function runs, which is exactly why 0125 printed slide 0x0.

The region then starts at SHARED_REGION_BASE_ARM64, check_np() returns the
nominal base, dyld derives slide == 0, and the unreslid contents match.  The
print shows both addresses so a boot log proves the arithmetic:

  MIDO SR 0126: noslide, slide 0x3514000 removed from 63 mapping(s) in 1
      file(s); first mapping 0x183514000 -> 0x180000000 (base 0x180000000)

diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_shared_region.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_shared_region.c
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_shared_region.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_shared_region.c
@@ -1961,30 +1961,74 @@
 
